+# BLOCKED: contradictory tests
+
+`test_slug.py` cannot pass as written. Two tests assert different results for
+the exact same input:
+
+- `test_preserves_underscores` (line 22-24):
+  `slugify("user_id field")` must equal `"user_id-field"` (spec 4.2).
+- `test_underscores_become_dashes` (line 26-28):
+  `slugify("user_id field")` must equal `"user-id-field"` (spec 4.5).
+
+A function is deterministic, so it cannot return both `"user_id-field"` and
+`"user-id-field"` for one input. The content team's URL spec must decide
+whether underscores are preserved or converted; only after that can the
+implementation match both tests.
+
+## What was done instead
+
+Everything else in the spec that the tests exercise was implemented in
+`slug.py` (lowercasing, punctuation stripping, dash collapsing, accent folding,
+trimming, and underscores-to-dashes). With that, 6 of 7 tests pass:
+
+```
+$ python3 -m unittest test_slug
+...F...
+FAIL: test_preserves_underscores
+Ran 7 tests
+FAILED (failures=1)
+```
+
+The remaining failure is solely the contradiction above. I chose
+"underscores become dashes" because it is consistent with spec 4.5's claim
+that slugs only contain `[a-z0-9-]`. No tests were modified.
